{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>At their sound they fled.</b> From this it appears that just as they were descending and being swallowed up in the earth, they were crying out for their lives — perhaps they were saying, 'Moshe is truth and his Torah is truth,' as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, mentioned in the episode of that Arab. Rabba bar bar Ḥanna said: Once I was walking on the road, and that Arab said to me, 'Come, let me show you the swallowed ones of Korah.' I saw two fissures from which smoke was rising. He took a ball of wool, soaked it in water, and placed it on the tip of a spear, and put it there and then drew it after. He said to me, 'Listen to what you hear.' And I heard them saying thus: 'Moshe is truth and his Torah is truth, and they are liars.' And know that this is indeed the sentence of the wicked in Gehinnom: to cry out in the midst of their torments and to justify the judgment upon themselves — therefore Gehinnom is called גי המין בו (the valley of those who answer in it)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase גי המין בו ('the valley of those who answer in it') appears to be a play on the name Gehinnom, understood as a place where the wicked 'answer' and confess the justice of their punishment; rendered literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:19.747988842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}